# ⚠ THIS FILE, NOT .dockerignore, CONTROLS WHAT CLOUD RUN UPLOADS.
#
# `gcloud run deploy --source .` uploads the WORKING DIRECTORY, not the tracked
# repository. With no .gcloudignore, gcloud derives its exclusions from
# .gitignore -- so any untracked, non-ignored file at the root goes to Cloud
# Build. That is not hypothetical: a stray `poetry.lock` in the working tree is
# a HIGH-PRECEDENCE package-manager marker, and Google's Python buildpack
# switches to Poetry the moment it sees one. This project has no [tool.poetry]
# section, so that path cannot succeed.
#
# Listing the exclusions explicitly makes the upload a property of the
# repository rather than of whatever happens to be lying around.

# --- version control ---
.git/
.gitignore
.gcloudignore

# --- python build/test detritus ---
.venv/
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
*.egg-info/
.pytest_cache/
.ruff_cache/

# --- ⚠ FOREIGN PACKAGE MANAGERS. Either one silently changes the build path. ---
poetry.lock
Pipfile
Pipfile.lock

# --- the dead Next.js skeleton. web/static IS required and stays. ---
node_modules/
.next/
web/app/
web/node_modules/
web/next.config.ts
web/package.json
web/tsconfig.json

# --- not needed by the running service ---
tests/
evals/results/
docs/shots/
docs/evidence/
.cache/
.github/

# ⚠ KEPT ON PURPOSE. Excluding any of these breaks the build or the service:
#   .python-version   pins the interpreter Cloud Build installs. Excluded, the
#                     buildpack silently reverts to "newest supported Python".
#   pyproject.toml    the dependency manifest pip reads
#   Procfile          the buildpack entrypoint
#   corpus/data/      spine.cascade reads it at request time
#   web/static/       the API serves the operator UI from it
#   evals/golden/     settle.cli reads court.txt
#   docs/COVERAGE.md  the coverage endpoint's committed artifact
